{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfdiy4ZQNvnEfnLFbgex3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with an overall verdict of **upheld**: I couldn't show any of the four B12 checks false. I only read files and wrote the verdict; I didn't run any scripts or the fixture.\n\n- **B12.1 holds.** The system prompt, classifier prompt, config and release manifest are all read from files under `CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT`. The Dockerfile sets that to `/app` and copies `prompts`, `config` and `release` into the image. Nothing is fetched from a URL, database or flag.\n- **B12.2 holds, but it's the weakest call.** `src/agent/` (the loop, classifier, budget and identity code) is owned only by the general dev team through `*`. It isn't covered by the platform leads' rules. Branch protection still requires code-owner review plus two approvals, so I treated it as covered. If you read \"cover\" as requiring platform-lead review of the harness code, this check fails on `.github/CODEOWNERS:3`.\n- **B12.3 holds.** Deploys run only through `workflow_dispatch` in the `production` or `production-emergency` environments, and both need lead approval. Production is limited to protected branches, and emergency deploys to `hotfix/*` with an owner, reason and expiry. The workflow verifies the image signature against `ci.yml` on `main` and records the git SHA and release on the deployment.\n- **B12.4 holds.** `main` blocks force-pushes and deletions, enforces the rules for admins, and requires signed commits and linear history. No bypass is configured."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1523,"cache_read_input_tokens":26623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1523},"output_tokens":516,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnosti